# Copy to .env for local hybrid-mode testing of the contact API:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   ADAPTER=node npm run build:server && npm run preview
#
# See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the full explanation of both build targets
# and how to deploy the hybrid (server) build.
#
# Pick ONE provider below. If both are set, Resend wins.
# If neither is set, /api/contact returns 503 and the contact form
# falls back to a mailto: link — this is also exactly what happens on
# the static GitHub Pages build, which never includes the route at all.

# --- Option A: Resend (recommended) ---------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=Portfolio Contact <onboarding@resend.dev>

# --- Option B: SMTP (any provider) -----------------------------------
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=you@example.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-smtp-password-or-app-token
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=you@example.com
